From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:09:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] exec: let seven's kernel hand sealed values to the
 command

When the environment fnox would give a command holds sealed secrets,
`fnox exec` resolves the command on PATH to a symlink-free path, sends
`materialize {names, path, argv, cwd}` to /dev/sealed with argv[0] set
to that path, and spawns exactly that program with argv and cwd,
every sealed variable set to its placeholder and SLICC_SEALED_TICKET
set to the ticket. The kernel swaps the placeholders it grants for
their values at exec; fnox never sees a value, and names the policy
keeps as placeholders are reported on stderr. On WASI, as_file secrets
are refused, values from other providers are passed as before with a
warning, and a command that is not found exits 127.

